  "brief": "EQT is acquiring Qiagen for €10.8 billion in an all-cash deal, while BASF is raising its offer for Evonik to €24 a share in a bid worth over €11 billion.\n\nEQT / Qiagen (Announced): EQT to Acquire Qiagen. EQT is acquiring Qiagen for €10.8 billion [3, 4, 6]. The deal was announced on October 22 [1, 2, 3]. No further information is available [4, 6].\nBASF / Evonik (Rumored): BASF Raises Evonik Offer. BASF is raising its offer for Evonik to €24 a share [12, 13, 16]. The bid is over €11 billion, according to Bloomberg [13, 16]. BASF's bid was rejected by Evonik earlier, but it's stepping up its push [14, 17].\nVivakor / Direct Midstream (Completed): Vivakor Acquires Direct Midstream. Vivakor has acquired Direct Midstream [18, 19]. The deal is now completed [18, 19].\nSalesforce / Braze (Announced): Salesforce to Acquire Braze. Salesforce is acquiring Braze in an all-cash deal worth $5.66 billion [20, 21, 22]. The deal was announced by Salesforce and has sent Braze's stock soaring [24, 25]. The acquisition is part of Salesforce's strategy to expand its customer engagement capabilities [26].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Rumored): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is in talks to buy Momentum Midstream for $5.5 billion [27, 28]. The deal is rumored to be worth $5.5 billion [27, 28].\nTechouse / Ambio (Announced): Techouse Acquires Ambio. Techouse has acquired Ambio [29, 30]. The acquisition expands Techouse's offshore water treatment business [29, 30].\nSpaceX / Tesla (Pending approval): SpaceX and Tesla Merger. The SpaceX and Tesla merger is pending approval and faces antitrust risks [31, 34, 35]. Analysts are split on the value of the deal, with some predicting a $480 billion and others a $550 billion valuation [33]. Elon Musk has expressed confidence in the deal, calling it a good idea [35]. Some predict a potential historic largest tech M&A deal, with one analyst suggesting a $420 billion acquisition [36].\nCentrus Energy / Westerman Acquisition (Announced): Centrus Energy and Westerman Acquisition. Centrus Energy and Westerman Acquisition is a deal where Centrus Energy acquires Westerman Acquisition [38, 37]. The deal was announced and no further updates are available [38].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- General Musk [39].\n- Realbotix Announces Additional Draw under Bridge Loan from Onconetix [40].\n- Weil’s Merger With Willkie Is Dead, But Its Partner Exodus Is Very Much Alive [41].",
